-- Repairs curly quotes and dashes garbled when the setup SQL was pasted (clipboard encoding).
-- ASCII-only on purpose. Safe to run more than once.

update public.products set title = U&'Polished Presence', subtitle = U&'Building A Brand That Cuts Through The Noise', description = U&'Your skills get clients in the chair. Your brand keeps them coming back \2014 and this book shows you exactly how to build one that lasts. Across 12 powerful chapters, it walks barbers and shop owners through every layer of brand building, from defining your core identity all the way to protecting and scaling your legacy as your business grows. It starts with a truth most barbers overlook: clients don\2019t just buy a haircut. They buy a feeling. A vibe. A promise. Your brand is that promise \2014 and without one, you\2019re just another room with chairs. No loyalty. No premium pricing. No lasting reputation. The book opens by reframing how you see branding entirely, making clear that it\2019s not just a logo or a color scheme \2014 it\2019s the psychology behind every single interaction you have with a client. From there, it guides you step by step. You\2019ll define your vision, mission, and core values. You\2019ll discover your niche \2014 because trying to be everything to everyone means being nothing to nobody. You\2019ll craft a shop name that\2019s memorable, unique, and aligned with who you are, then build a visual identity with intentional colors, logos, and brand guidelines that create instant recognition and trust. Your brand voice gets its own chapter \2014 because how you text a client, caption an Instagram post, or respond to a complaint all reflect who you are as a business. Consistency in your voice builds credibility. And credibility builds loyalty. The book goes beyond the digital and into the physical \2014 teaching you how to design your shop space as a branding tool in itself. Lighting, music, furniture, and even the scent of your shop all contribute to the experience your clients carry with them long after they leave. Every sensory detail is an opportunity to reinforce who you are. You\2019ll also learn how to align your personal brand with your business identity, build a team that embodies your values, and create systems that deliver the same exceptional experience every single time \2014 whether you\2019re behind the chair or not. And when it\2019s time to evolve, the book has you covered \2014 guiding you through a confident rebrand without losing the loyal clients you\2019ve already earned. A brand built right today doesn\2019t just fill your calendar. It creates income, commands respect, and builds a legacy that outlives you.' where slug = 'polished-presence';
update public.products set title = U&'First Impressions Matter', subtitle = U&'Free Chapter', description = U&'Download \201cFirst Impressions Matter\201d from Before The Cut \2014 free. Learn how your grooming, station, tone, and presence already tell clients everything they need to know. Instant PDF \2014 no spam, just one powerful chapter.' where slug = 'first-impressions-matter';
update public.products set title = U&'Rent the Chair or Own the Shop', subtitle = U&'Making the Right Move in Your Career', description = U&'Booth Rental vs. Ownership \2014 Choosing the Right Path for Your Career Every barber and stylist reaches a point where the chair starts feeling too small. The question is \2014 what\2019s your next move? Across 13 focused chapters, this book helps beauty professionals make one of the most important career decisions of their lives with clarity, confidence, and a clear-eyed understanding of what each path truly demands. It starts where every smart decision starts \2014 with self-awareness. Before you sign a lease or rent a chair, you need to know who you are, what drives you, and where you want to be in one, three, and five years. From there, the book breaks down both paths honestly and thoroughly \2014 the freedom and flexibility of booth rental, and the power and pressure of full ownership \2014 without romanticizing either one. Every chapter delivers practical, real-world guidance. You\2019ll compare income models, understand tax and legal obligations, navigate lease negotiations, build your brand, and learn what it actually takes to lead a team. Location strategy, scaling plans, and the psychology of your workspace all get their own dedicated attention. Real stories from professionals who rented, owned, downsized, and pivoted bring the lessons to life \2014 raw, relatable, and refreshingly honest. The book closes with a personalized decision matrix to help you weigh your options based on your unique situation, not someone else\2019s blueprint. Because there\2019s no single right path in this industry. There\2019s only the one that\2019s right for you \2014 and this book helps you find it.' where slug = 'rent-the-chair-or-own-the-shop';
update public.products set title = U&'The Art of Building Your Clientele in the Barber and Beauty Industry', subtitle = U&'', description = U&'Building a Thriving Career in the Barber and Beauty Industry. This book is your complete roadmap to building not just a full client base \2014 but a lasting, fulfilling career that stands the test of time. Across 10 practical chapters, it covers every dimension of what it truly takes to succeed behind the chair, from the very first impression all the way to long-term financial planning and avoiding burnout. It opens where every client relationship begins \2014 that split-second first impression. Your appearance, your energy, your greeting, and your environment all speak before you ever pick up a clipper. From there, it guides you through building a professional persona that\2019s uniquely yours, finding your specialty, and showing up consistently both online and in person. Consistency is treated as a superpower throughout the book. Clients return to barbers and stylists they can predict and trust \2014 and you\2019ll learn how to build systems, routines, and communication habits that make every experience feel reliable and intentional. The book then dives into growing your business organically \2014 through referrals, social media content, community involvement, and loyalty programs that make clients feel genuinely valued. You\2019ll also learn how to price your services with confidence, handle difficult clients professionally, and respond to reviews in a way that protects your brand. The final chapter zooms out \2014 encouraging you to track your numbers, invest in your education, diversify your income streams, and plan for your future. Because a great barber builds a great career \2014 but a smart barber builds a great life.' where slug = 'the-art-of-building-your-clientele-in-the-barber-and-beauty-industry';
update public.products set title = U&'From Walk-In to Locked In', subtitle = U&'How Barbers and Stylists Can Turn First Time Clients into Loyalists', description = U&'This book is a powerful, practical roadmap for barbers and stylists who want to stop chasing clients and start keeping them \2014 for life. Across 15 carefully crafted chapters, it walks you through every touchpoint of the client experience, from the moment someone walks through your door to the moment they\2019re raving about you to their friends. Whether you\2019re a mobile barber, shop owner, or independent stylist, this guide treats your craft not just as a skill \2014 but as a business, a relationship, and a legacy. It starts before the first cut. The opening chapters zero in on the Golden 60 Seconds \2014 that critical window when a new client decides whether they trust you. You\2019ll learn how to engineer your environment, your energy, and your greeting to make every walk-in feel like a VIP. Then comes the consultation \2014 the most underrated skill in the industry. Asking the right questions before you pick up a clipper prevents misunderstandings, saves money, and builds instant trust. Confidence during the cut is contagious. The book explores how your vibe behind the chair directly impacts how your client feels in it \2014 and how narrating your process, handling feedback gracefully, and moving with intention positions you as a true professional. The mirror reveal is treated as the emotional climax of the entire appointment, and you\2019ll learn how to present your work with pride while planting seeds for the next visit. Emotional intelligence separates good barbers from great ones. A full chapter dives into reading the room, navigating sensitive conversations, and protecting your energy \2014 because true loyalty is built not just through skill, but through making people feel genuinely seen and respected. From there, the book gets deeply practical. You\2019ll build repeatable systems using the \201c3 P\2019s\201d \2014 Professionalism, Presence, and Personalization. You\2019ll master the art of remembering client names, styles, and stories. You\2019ll learn how to rebook confidently, follow up within 24 hours, and create a sensory environment that clients want to photograph and share. Not every client is your client. The book teaches you to recognize different personalities, spot red flags early, and professionally decline relationships that drain your energy. And when mistakes happen \2014 because they will \2014 you\2019ll have the scripts and mindset to turn errors into loyalty-building moments. The final chapters make the case that retention always beats volume. A focused, loyal clientele is more profitable than constantly chasing walk-ins. You\2019ll learn how to generate referrals naturally, fill your books during slow seasons, and build the kind of demand that makes clients happy to wait for you. This book ends where every great career should \2014 with legacy. Not just a full calendar, but a reputation, a community, and a career that truly means something. This isn\2019t just about hair. It\2019s about building a business that runs on trust \2014 one client at a time.' where slug = 'from-walk-in-to-locked-in';
update public.products set title = U&'GSWAU Barber Success Bundle', subtitle = U&'', description = U&'Stop leaving money on the table. The GSWAU Barber Success Bundle gives you 5 powerful books that turn talented barbers and stylists into real business owners. Get: \2022 Booked and Busy (Marketing that fills chairs) \2022 From Posts to Profits (Build your brand online) \2022 Before The Cut (Master client consultations) \2022 Cutting Edge Leadership (Run a thriving shop) \2022 Cut and Go (Mobile barber playbook) Everything you need to get booked, build loyalty, and make money beyond the chair. Normally much more \2014 now only $97. Instant download. Start winning today.' where slug = 'gswau-barber-success-bundle';
update public.products set title = U&'Haircuts Without The Headaches', subtitle = U&'', description = U&'This book is the survival guide every barber and stylist needs but rarely gets. While most industry training focuses on technique \2014 the perfect fade, the flawless color \2014 this one tackles something far more complex: the human side of the business. The conversations, the conflicts, the complaints, and the emotional weight that comes with serving people for a living. Across 10 powerful chapters, it equips you with the mindset, the scripts, and the strategies to handle every difficult situation behind the chair with professionalism, confidence, and grace. It starts where every service starts \2014 the first impression. But beyond the warm welcome, it teaches you to read the room immediately. Is this client going to be cooperative, or are there warning signs hiding in plain sight? Something as simple as how they talk about their last barber can tell you everything you need to know before you even pick up a clipper. The book teaches you to trust those instincts and act on them early. From there, it introduces you to the most common problem client personalities \2014 the Chronic Complainer, the Micromanager, the Vague Visionary, the Entitled One, and the dreaded No-Show Repeat Offender. Each type is broken down with real-world examples and proactive strategies so you\2019re never caught off guard. Knowing who\2019s sitting in your chair changes everything about how you approach the service. Active listening is the skill that holds it all together. Truly hearing your client goes far beyond nodding along. It means repeating details back for confirmation, decoding vague requests like \201cjust a little off the top,\201d and using photo references to eliminate guesswork. When communication is crystal clear from the start, complaints become rare and trust builds naturally. But when clients are difficult \2014 and they will be \2014 you\2019ll learn how to stay professional no matter what. Breathing techniques, mindful body language, and verbal judo give you practical tools to de-escalate tension without losing your composure or your authority. Complaints, when handled correctly, can actually strengthen loyalty. The book walks you through a four-step recovery process \2014 apologize, acknowledge, offer a solution, and follow up \2014 showing how a dissatisfied client can become your most passionate supporter when you respond with calm and genuine care. Boundaries are not optional \2014 they are your business. You\2019ll find real scripts for saying no politely, communicating your policies from day one, and confidently handling requests for discounts or extra services without compensation. Consistent boundaries don\2019t drive good clients away. They attract better ones and filter out the ones who were never a right fit to begin with. Sometimes, the relationship simply has to end. The book gives you the language and the courage to professionally part ways with clients who are damaging your well-being \2014 without unnecessary drama, without guilt, and without putting your reputation at risk. It also addresses the modern challenge of online reviews and social media conflicts, offering clear response templates and guidance on when to engage publicly and when silence is the stronger move. The final chapters bring it all home \2014 reminding you that you don\2019t have to carry the weight of difficult clients alone. Team support, shared policies, and strong leadership all play a role in creating a healthier work environment. And perhaps most importantly, the book closes with a deep focus on your mental health \2014 helping you recognize burnout before it takes over, build daily routines that keep you grounded, and remember that your peace is not a luxury. It is the foundation everything else is built on. Technical skill gets you in the door. Emotional intelligence keeps you in business \2014 and keeps you well while you\2019re doing it.' where slug = 'haircuts-without-the-headaches';
update public.products set title = U&'Profits beyond the chair', subtitle = U&'', description = U&'The Digital Barber: Building Your Brand, Business, and Income Online The barber game has changed \2014 and this book makes sure you\2019re ahead of it. Across 10 action-packed chapters, it walks barbers through everything they need to build a powerful online presence, sell products, attract new clients, and create income streams that work even when they\2019re not standing behind the chair. It starts with the mindset shift: going digital isn\2019t optional anymore. Competition is fierce, clients expect convenience, and the barbers winning right now are the ones who\2019ve figured out how to turn their craft into a brand. From building a clean, professional website to setting up online booking, launching a product line, and mastering social media \2014 every chapter gives you practical, step-by-step guidance without overwhelming technical jargon. You\2019ll learn how to sell physical products like pomades, oils, and branded merchandise, explore options like private label, affiliate marketing, and dropshipping, and even offer virtual consultations and online courses that generate income around the clock. Social media strategy, video content creation, email marketing, text campaigns, and client retention systems all get their own dedicated chapters \2014 complete with real examples and beginner-friendly tools. The book closes by thinking big \2014 global shipping, brand partnerships, passive income, and building a team to support your growing digital empire. Because the best barbers today aren\2019t just great with clippers. They\2019re building brands, businesses, and legacies that extend far beyond the chair.' where slug = 'profits-beyond-the-chair';
update public.products set title = U&'From Posts to Profits', subtitle = U&'Building Your Brand Online As A Barber Or A Stylist', description = U&'From Post To Profits: Building Your Brand Online as a Barber or Stylist is the ultimate digital playbook for beauty professionals who are ready to turn their social media presence into a real, thriving business. In today\2019s world, your next client isn\2019t finding you through word of mouth alone \2014 they\2019re scrolling, searching, and making decisions about you before they ever send that first DM. The question is: what are they finding when they look? This guide takes you step by step through everything you need to build a powerful, profitable online brand from the ground up. You\2019ll start by auditing your current digital presence and defining what makes you uniquely you \2014 your voice, your energy, your aesthetic, and the story only you can tell. From crafting the perfect bio to building a full brand board, you\2019ll walk away knowing exactly who you are online and who you\2019re speaking to. You\2019ll learn how to identify your ideal client, choose the right platforms for your brand, and create content that actually converts \2014 not just gets likes. Discover the power of before-and-after transformations, behind-the-scenes content, client spotlights, and video Reels that stop the scroll and fill your booking calendar. Master hashtags, captions, and the algorithm so your work gets seen by the people who matter most. But this book goes beyond just posting. You\2019ll learn how to turn DMs into booked appointments, collect glowing reviews that build instant trust, and set up seamless booking systems that work even while you sleep. And when you\2019re ready to scale, you\2019ll explore how to grow from stylist to CEO \2014 with digital courses, product lines, and a brand that extends far beyond the chair. Consistency beats clout every single time. This book will show you how to build a sustainable online strategy that grows with you \2014 without burning you out. Your chair is your stage. Your phone is your megaphone. Now it\2019s time to use both with purpose.' where slug = 'from-posts-to-profits';
update public.products set title = U&'Inventory Management for Barbershops and Salons', subtitle = U&'', description = U&'Your Guide to Painless Inventory for Barbershops and Salons You\2019re a pro behind the chair \2014 but the business side? That\2019s where most barbers and stylists struggle. This book fixes that. Across 13 practical chapters, it breaks down everything you need to know about managing your products, tools, and supplies without the stress, the waste, or the guesswork. From categorizing your backbar and retail products to setting smart par levels, building reorder schedules, and running regular audits \2014 every system is laid out in simple, actionable steps. You\2019ll learn how to stop over-ordering, eliminate waste, negotiate with vendors, and turn your retail shelf into a serious income stream that can boost revenue by 15-25% or more. It also tackles the tough stuff \2014 theft prevention, team accountability, tool maintenance, and scaling your system when you\2019re ready to grow. Whether you\2019re a solo mobile barber or managing a multi-chair shop, this guide meets you where you are. The bottom line is simple: inventory chaos costs you money, clients, and peace of mind. But with the right systems in place, you\2019re not just a talented barber or stylist anymore. You\2019re a CEO who knows their numbers \2014 and that changes everything.' where slug = 'inventory-management-for-barbershops-and-salons';
update public.products set title = U&'Its more than just a haircut use product selling principles', subtitle = U&'', description = U&'The service doesn\2019t end when your client leaves the chair \2014 and this book makes that crystal clear. Across 12 focused chapters, it teaches barbers and stylists how to naturally recommend the right products, build genuine client trust, and boost retail income without ever feeling pushy, awkward, or salesy. This is the guide that bridges the gap between a great haircut and a great hair day \2014 every single day. It starts with a simple but powerful truth: your clients go home and struggle to recreate what you just did. The style falls flat. The texture disappears. The confidence fades. The right product recommendation closes that gap and positions you as more than a skilled technician \2014 it makes you a trusted hair advisor who shows up for your clients even when they\2019re not in your chair. From understanding buyer psychology to planting seeds early in the consultation, every chapter gives you real scripts, practical techniques, and honest strategies. You\2019ll learn how to read body language, ask the right questions, and introduce products naturally mid-service \2014 long before the client is heading for the door. The book teaches you to think like a hair doctor: diagnose the problem, then prescribe the solution. You\2019ll learn how to customize recommendations by hair type and lifestyle, demonstrate products chairside so clients can see and feel the results firsthand, handle objections with empathy, and design a retail space that invites browsing and encourages buying. It even covers building simple take-home routines that clients will actually follow, and how to follow up after the appointment to reinforce your recommendations and strengthen the relationship. The message throughout is consistent and clear \2014 prescribe, don\2019t push. When your recommendations come from a place of genuine expertise and real care, clients don\2019t feel sold to. They feel guided, supported, and empowered. And empowered clients rebook, refer friends, and buy \2014 every single time.' where slug = 'its-more-than-just-a-haircut-use-product-selling-principles';
update public.products set title = U&'No English No Problem', subtitle = U&'Mastering Nonverbal and Visual Communication in the Shop', description = U&'Mastering Nonverbal Communication for Barbers and Stylists In today\2019s diverse world, your clients don\2019t always speak your language \2014 but that should never stop you from delivering an exceptional experience. Across 12 powerful chapters, this book teaches barbers and stylists how to communicate confidently and effectively without saying a single word. From mastering gestures and reading body language to building visual style boards, using digital translation tools, and designing an inclusive shop environment, every chapter gives you practical skills to bridge any language gap with professionalism and warmth. You\2019ll learn how to conduct a full client consultation using nothing but photos, hand gestures, and mirror confirmations \2014 and how to spot and fix miscommunication before it becomes a bad haircut. The book also tackles the emotional side \2014 understanding what a nervous, non-English-speaking client feels when they sit in your chair, and how simple acts of patience, calm energy, and genuine care speak louder than any words ever could. Whether you\2019re serving immigrants, tourists, or anyone who feels more comfortable staying quiet, this guide turns what most barbers see as a barrier into your biggest competitive advantage. Because when you can connect with anyone \2014 regardless of language \2014 you don\2019t just build a clientele. You build a community.' where slug = 'no-english-no-problem';
update public.products set title = U&'The Barbers Toolkit', subtitle = U&'', description = U&'A Barber\2019s Complete Guide to Tools, Maintenance, and Mastery. Your skills are only as good as the tools in your hands \2014 and this book makes sure those tools are always ready to perform. Across 10 focused chapters, it walks barbers at every level through everything they need to know about their gear, from building the perfect starter kit to embracing the latest innovations in barbering technology. It starts with the essentials \2014 clippers, shears, razors, edgers, combs, and brushes \2014 breaking down each tool\2019s purpose, strengths, and best use cases so you can build a kit that truly matches your style and technique. Whether you\2019re a beginner figuring out your first setup or a seasoned pro looking to level up, every chapter meets you where you are. From there, the book goes deeper \2014 covering blade maintenance, daily and weekly cleaning routines, proper sanitation, and how to organize your station for maximum efficiency and flow. Because a clean, organized workspace isn\2019t just professional \2014 it\2019s a direct reflection of your brand. Specialized chapters tackle fades, beard sculpting, mobile setups, and the smart decision of when to repair versus replace aging tools. The book closes with a fascinating look at how barbering technology has evolved \2014 from classic straight razors to quiet motors, wireless charging, and vacuum clipper systems. Because behind every great cut is a barber who respects their craft \2014 and that starts with knowing, caring for, and mastering every single tool in their hands.' where slug = 'the-barbers-toolkit';
update public.products set title = U&'The Price Shift', subtitle = U&'A Barbers and Stylist\2019s Guide to Price Increase By G.S. W. Augustin', description = U&'Know Your Worth: The Barber and Stylist\2019s Complete Guide to Confident Pricing Undercharging isn\2019t humility \2014 it\2019s a habit that quietly drains your energy, your income, and your passion for the craft. Across 14 focused chapters, this book gives barbers and stylists everything they need to price their services with confidence, communicate increases without apology, and build a business that genuinely reflects their value. It starts where every pricing problem starts \2014 in your head. Fear of losing clients, guilt around money, and imposter syndrome are real barriers, and this book tackles them head-on with mindset work, affirmations, journaling exercises, and real stories from professionals who raised their prices and watched their businesses grow. From there, it dives into the psychology of pricing \2014 why higher prices actually build trust, why discounting devalues your brand, and how your price tag communicates your positioning before a client ever sits down. You\2019ll learn exactly when to raise your prices, how to calculate your real hourly cost, how to structure packages and memberships, and how to communicate increases to clients with scripts that are direct, confident, and never apologetic. The book also prepares you for pushback \2014 with ready-to-use responses for every objection \2014 and gives you permission to gracefully release clients who no longer fit your business. Branding, image, service upgrades, tracking key metrics, and planning for future increases round out a guide that\2019s as practical as it is empowering. Because charging what you\2019re worth isn\2019t about money. It\2019s about respect \2014 for your craft, your time, and your legacy.' where slug = 'the-price-shift';
update public.products set title = U&'Cut and Go', subtitle = U&'The Mobile Barbers Playbook for Building a Mobile Empire', description = U&'This book is a complete blueprint for barbers who want to break free from the traditional shop model and build a successful mobile barber business. It explains why mobile barbering is one of the fastest-growing opportunities in the industry, giving professionals more freedom, flexible schedules, higher earning potential, and direct access to premium clients who value convenience. Readers will learn how to choose and design the right mobile setup, from vans and trailers to portable event stations, while creating a clean, professional experience clients trust. The book also covers licensing, insurance, legal protection, and the must-have tools needed to deliver high-quality cuts on the go. Beyond operations, it teaches branding strategies to turn your vehicle into a rolling advertisement and build a recognizable business that stands out. Marketing chapters show how to attract clients through social media, Google listings, referrals, and local partnerships. Readers will also master booking systems, route planning, and scheduling to maximize time and profits. The client experience is a major focus, teaching how to create luxury-level service, build loyalty, and generate repeat customers. Advanced chapters explore weddings, VIP events, corporate contracts, and pop-up opportunities that can dramatically increase income. Finally, the book reveals how to grow from one vehicle into a fleet, hire other barbers, create systems, and build a long-term brand that generates wealth. Whether you\2019re a beginner or experienced barber, this guide shows how to transform your skills into a mobile empire.' where slug = 'cut-and-go';
update public.products set title = U&'The People\2019s Shop', subtitle = U&'Designing a Place Where Clients Feel At Home', description = U&'More Than a Haircut: Building an Inclusive, Community-Centered Barbershop The most successful barbershops have always been more than places to get a cut \2014 they\2019ve been community hubs, safe spaces, and neighborhood landmarks. Across 12 powerful chapters, this book shows you exactly how to build that kind of shop intentionally, with systems, culture, and values that make every single client feel genuinely welcome from the moment they walk through the door. It covers every layer of the client experience \2014 from your exterior signage and lighting to your greeting scripts, seating comfort, playlist strategy, and the words you use in the chair. You\2019ll learn how to serve every hair type with confidence, use inclusive language, handle complaints professionally, and design a physical space that works for clients with disabilities, sensory needs, and diverse cultural backgrounds. Beyond the individual experience, the book builds outward \2014 helping you curate d\00e9cor that reflects your community, host events that create real impact, build a team that lives your values, and establish partnerships that extend your shop\2019s reach far beyond your four walls. Every chapter is packed with action plans, role-play exercises, quick checklists, and ready-to-use templates so that nothing stays theoretical. This is a hands-on guide built for immediate results. The message throughout is clear and consistent: inclusivity isn\2019t a trend or a marketing strategy. It\2019s the foundation of a thriving, loyal, and respected business. Because when everyone feels welcome in your chair, everyone keeps coming back.' where slug = 'the-people-s-shop';
update public.products set title = U&'The Science of the Scalp Behind the Chair', subtitle = U&'', description = U&'Beneath the Cut: The Barber and Stylist\2019s Complete Guide to Scalp Health Most barbers and stylists are trained to perfect the cut \2014 but few are trained to truly understand what\2019s happening underneath it. Across 12 in-depth chapters, this book transforms the way beauty professionals see the scalp, turning everyday service into a genuine act of health-conscious care. It starts with a powerful truth: barbers and stylists are often the first people to notice changes on a client\2019s scalp \2014 before a doctor, before a dermatologist, before anyone. That proximity is a responsibility, and this book gives you the knowledge to honor it. From understanding the anatomy of the scalp and hair follicle to recognizing common conditions like dandruff, psoriasis, folliculitis, ringworm, and the various forms of hair loss \2014 every chapter builds your ability to see what others miss and respond with confidence and professionalism. You\2019ll learn how stress, hormones, diet, medications, and even product buildup show up on the scalp, and how to open those conversations with clients in a way that feels caring rather than alarming. The book also covers chemical and heat damage, texture-specific scalp needs, proper sanitation practices, and when to gently refer a client to a medical professional. Natural remedies, professional scalp treatments, and strategies for adding scalp health services to your menu round out a guide that\2019s as business-savvy as it is educational. Because the best barbers and stylists don\2019t just perfect the look on top. They understand and protect everything beneath it.' where slug = 'the-science-of-the-scalp-behind-the-chair';
update public.products set title = U&'Cut The Noise', subtitle = U&'The Barbers & Stylists Guide To Listening Behind The Chair', description = U&'Cut The Noise: The Barber and Stylist\2019s Guide to Listening Behind the Chair is the game-changing book the beauty industry has been missing. Beyond the fade and the finish, what truly separates good barbers from great ones is the ability to really listen. This guide takes you deep into the art of active listening \2014 teaching you how to read body language, decode what clients aren\2019t saying, ask questions that build genuine trust, and create an atmosphere where people feel safe and valued. From handling nervous first-timers to managing difficult conversations with grace, every chapter equips you with real, practical tools to elevate your client experience. Learn how silence can be your strongest asset, how listening drives loyalty, and how one meaningful conversation can turn a walk-in into a lifelong client. Whether you\2019re behind the chair or leading a team, this book will transform the way you connect. Because the most powerful tool in your shop isn\2019t your clippers \2014 it\2019s your ears.' where slug = 'cut-the-noise';
update public.products set title = U&'Cutting Stress, Not Just Hair', subtitle = U&'A Barber\2019s & Stylist\2019s Burnout Survival Guide', description = U&'Cutting Stress, Not Just Hair: A Barber and Stylist\2019s Burnout Survival Guide is the honest, no-nonsense book this industry has needed for a long time. From the outside, life behind the chair looks glamorous \2014 the creativity, the community, the craft. But the reality tells a different story. The long hours on your feet, the physical strain on your body, the emotional weight of client conversations, and the constant pressure to perform at your best every single day takes a serious toll. Burnout isn\2019t a personal failure \2014 it\2019s a predictable result of an industry that too often glorifies the grind and ignores the human behind the scissors. This guide is your roadmap back to yourself. You\2019ll learn how to spot the early warning signs of burnout before they cost you your career \2014 the chronic exhaustion, the cynicism, the loss of joy in work you once loved. You\2019ll understand the gap between the polished highlight reel of social media and the real, emotionally draining week happening behind the scenes. And most importantly, you\2019ll get the practical tools to do something about it. From setting firm boundaries without guilt, to protecting your body with ergonomic habits and daily mobility routines \2014 this book covers it all. Discover how to work smarter with better pricing strategies, build rest into your schedule without losing momentum, and handle clients who bring heavy emotional baggage to your chair without carrying it home with you. But this isn\2019t just about surviving \2014 it\2019s about thriving. You\2019ll reignite your creative spark, design a long-term career path that prioritizes your health and well-being, and learn how to build a shop culture that lifts the next generation up instead of burning them out. Whether you\2019re running on empty right now or just starting to feel the weight of the grind, this book will meet you exactly where you are and walk you toward a career that lasts. Your passion brought you to this industry. This guide will help you stay.' where slug = 'cutting-stress-not-just-hair';
update public.products set title = U&'Crafted by the Chair', subtitle = U&'A Barber\2019s Transformation from Apprentice to Becoming a Master Barber', description = U&'This book is a complete roadmap for anyone who wants to build a successful career in barbering\2014from beginner to master barber. It goes far beyond learning how to cut hair by teaching the mindset, discipline, technical skills, business knowledge, and leadership needed to thrive in the industry. Readers will learn how to discover their purpose, develop professionalism, master fades, lineups, shaves, beard work, consultations, client communication, speed, precision, and signature styles that make them stand out. The book also breaks down the business side of barbering, including pricing, branding, marketing, booking systems, client retention, referrals, finances, and scaling into shop ownership or multiple income streams. It teaches how to create a personal brand, use social media effectively, build loyal clientele, and turn barbering skills into long-term wealth and freedom. Beyond the chair, it explores mentorship, teaching others, community impact, partnerships, content creation, and expanding influence outside the shop. It emphasizes character, consistency, hygiene, work ethic, and leaving a positive legacy in the barber industry. Whether you are just starting, currently apprenticing, or already cutting hair and wanting to level up, this book provides practical strategies, drills, systems, and real-world wisdom to sharpen both your craft and your career. It is not just about becoming a better barber\2014it is about becoming a respected professional, entrepreneur, and leader whose name carries value for years to come.' where slug = 'crafted-by-the-chair';
update public.products set title = U&'The Legacy of the Chair', subtitle = U&'Passing Skills, Standards, and Style to the Next Generation for Barbers and Stylists', description = U&'A Complete Guide to Mentorship in the Barber and Beauty Industry. This book is for every barber and stylist who has mastered their craft and is ready to pass it on. Across 12 powerful chapters, it builds a complete mentorship system \2014 from teaching core technical skills all the way to creating a lasting legacy that outlives your time behind the chair. It opens with a truth the industry doesn\2019t talk about enough: mentorship isn\2019t just generous \2014 it\2019s essential. It preserves standards, strengthens reputations, builds better teams, and protects the culture of the craft. From there, it guides experienced barbers and stylists through every stage of the mentorship journey \2014 understanding how people learn, developing the right mindset, teaching with structure, instilling professionalism, and building confidence in someone who is just finding their voice. Every chapter is packed with practical tools \2014 lesson plan templates, skills matrices, feedback frameworks, sanitation drills, consent scripts, and confidence ladders \2014 so mentorship never feels vague or overwhelming. You\2019ll learn how to give feedback that lands, handle mistakes with calm and purpose, teach your signature techniques without cloning yourself, and prepare your mentee for full career independence. The final chapter elevates the entire conversation \2014 pushing you to codify your knowledge, train other mentors, and launch a legacy project that keeps your craft alive for generations to come. Because the greatest cut you\2019ll ever make isn\2019t on a client. It\2019s in the career of someone you believed in.' where slug = 'the-legacy-of-the-chair';

